  "question": {
    "text": "Each of the two inputs $A$ and $B$ can assume values either 0 or 1. Then which of the following will be equal to $\\bar{A} \\cdot \\bar{B} ?$"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$A+B$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{}{A+B}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{}{A \\cdot B}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\bar{A}+\\bar{B}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "By using the de-Morgan's law\r\n$$\r\n\\overline{A+B}=\\overline{A \\cdot B}\r\n$$\r\nHence, option (b) is the correct."
  }
}